grid: 10 widths x 2 policies = 20 named primitives per family

CONTROL distinct-family : 20 bodies + 0 aliases (want 20 bodies, 0 aliases)
CONTROL identical-family: 0 bodies + 20 aliases (want 0 bodies, 20 aliases, 1 distinct target); targets = ['_d_wrap_13']
controls: ok

object file size: 1744 bytes
asm lines       : 189

READING: naming N genuinely-different primitives costs N machine bodies.
         naming N primitives that compute what some existing body already
         computes costs ZERO additional bodies: all N become aliases of it,
         across family boundaries. Here 40 named primitives -> 20 bodies.
         The cost of a name tracks what its body computes, never the name,
         and never the number of type parameters that produced it.
